<title>USA: FSA qualifies nine muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies nine muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said it has qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Kings Mountain, N.C., $7.02 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Washington Township, N.J., $6 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cortland, N.Y., $2.5 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Rotterdam CSD, N.Y., $2.37 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Philipsburg Area School District, Pa., $7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Minneapolis Special School District No.1, Minn., $47.4 million school building GOs.</p>
<p>--East Rockaway, N.Y., $1.540 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Park City School District, Utah, school building GOs</p>
<p>--Mauston, Wis., $1.575 million refunding GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
